what is Scout Mastership anyway?

61
00:03:11,700 --> 00:03:12,020
Yeah,

62
00:03:12,960 --> 00:03:14,280
A little talk about that.

63
00:03:14,820 --> 00:03:17,240
Then I've got an email question to answer

64
00:03:18,180 --> 00:03:22,600
and a post that went on the blog this week

65
00:03:22,600 --> 00:03:25,520
that got several good comments that I wanted to talk about.

66
00:03:25,520 --> 00:03:29,400
So that's a lot to do.

67
00:03:29,840 --> 00:03:30,960
Let's get started, shall we?

68
00:03:31,680 --> 00:03:36,120
Scout Mastership in seven minutes or less.

69
00:03:36,120 --> 00:03:45,500
You know whenever I type the word Scout Mastership

70
00:03:45,500 --> 00:03:48,820
into my computer,

71
00:03:49,620 --> 00:03:51,900
the spell checker underlines it in red.

72
00:03:53,400 --> 00:03:55,860
It's just not a common term, is it

73
00:03:56,640 --> 00:03:57,840
Scout Mastership?

74
00:03:57,840 --> 00:04:02,060
My best guess is that it was probably coined by Baden-Powell

75
00:04:02,060 --> 00:04:05,980
in the title of his little booklet

76
00:04:06,660 --> 00:04:08,040
Aids to Scout Mastership.

77
00:04:09,120 --> 00:04:10,860
Dictionaries don't recognize that word,

78
00:04:12,460 --> 00:04:14,100
But Scout Mastership the word.

79
00:04:15,160 --> 00:04:18,180
I like it because I think it embodies an important concept

80
00:04:18,180 --> 00:04:20,840
that differentiates the work of Scouting in general

81
00:04:21,519 --> 00:04:22,980
and Scout Masters in particular

82
00:04:23,100 --> 00:04:26,360
from other forms of leadership and administration and management.

83
00:04:26,360 --> 00:04:30,040
You know we can find some inspiration and practical advice

84
00:04:30,040 --> 00:04:31,440
in the study of business management

85
00:04:31,440 --> 00:04:35,000
and you know leadership books and things like that,

86
00:04:35,440 --> 00:04:38,460
And we can certainly adapt a lot of those concepts

87
00:04:38,460 --> 00:04:42,160
into the unique practice of Scout Mastership.

88
00:04:42,220 --> 00:04:43,760
But, as we've talked about before,

89
00:04:44,640 --> 00:04:46,960
we're not responsible for the production of a product

90
00:04:46,960 --> 00:04:51,160
or the management of easily quantified numerical goals

91
00:04:52,140 --> 00:04:55,140
And we're not charged with administering a program

92
00:04:55,140 --> 00:04:56,979
or maintaining a set of standards.

93
00:04:58,419 --> 00:05:01,680
I think Scout Mastership has elements of teaching

94
00:05:01,680 --> 00:05:04,360
and parenting and mentoring and leading and managing

95
00:05:04,360 --> 00:05:05,340
and administering.

96
00:05:05,500 --> 00:05:09,380
yet it defies definition

97
00:05:09,380 --> 00:05:12,380
of any one of those single fields.

98
00:05:13,260 --> 00:05:17,159
The term Scout Mastership sets us apart

99
00:05:17,159 --> 00:05:20,500
and sets the role apart as a pretty unique endeavor.

100
00:05:20,500 --> 00:05:24,520
Scout Masters mentor Scouts through a variety of experiences

101
00:05:24,520 --> 00:05:27,340
in such a way that they learn for themselves

102
00:05:27,340 --> 00:05:31,860
and they weave together all the various influences in their lives.

103
00:05:32,220 --> 00:05:36,820
We're given a more general inspiration as Scout Masters

104
00:05:36,820 --> 00:05:39,580
than a lot of specific directions,

105
00:05:40,280 --> 00:05:41,940
And purposefully so,

106
00:05:42,300 --> 00:05:45,500
because each one of us will have a slightly different way

107
00:05:45,500 --> 00:05:46,700
of carrying out the work.

108
00:05:46,700 --> 00:05:51,539
A great revelation for Scout Masters

109
00:05:51,539 --> 00:05:53,219
is the discovery that there's no

110
00:05:53,219 --> 00:05:57,460
universally adaptable, step-by-step plan for scouting,

111
00:05:57,860 --> 00:06:00,700
but rather well-expressed

112
00:06:00,700 --> 00:06:03,099
yet potentially frustrating generalizations.

113
00:06:04,780 --> 00:06:05,820
Here's an example:

114
00:06:05,940 --> 00:06:07,840
Is every Eagle Scout identical in character

115
00:06:07,840 --> 00:06:10,020
and deportment to every other Eagle Scout?

116
00:06:10,520 --> 00:06:13,180
Does every troop operate under a universal,

117
00:06:13,180 --> 00:06:15,220
specific method of administration?

118
00:06:15,600 --> 00:06:16,880
Well, you can say yes,

119
00:06:17,400 --> 00:06:20,140
but you know everybody's going to handle it

120
00:06:20,140 --> 00:06:20,920
a little bit differently.

121
00:06:22,020 --> 00:06:24,040
Is every Scout equally talented?

122
00:06:24,780 --> 00:06:28,160
Do they all share the same disposition and outlook?

123
00:06:28,900 --> 00:06:30,820
Well, there's a lot of common points,

124
00:06:30,960 --> 00:06:32,600
but every single one of them is different.

125
00:06:33,140 --> 00:06:36,440
I think what might help understand this

126
00:06:36,440 --> 00:06:40,500
is something expressed by the diplomat

127
00:06:40,860 --> 00:06:41,860
Carl Schurz.

128
00:06:41,860 --> 00:06:43,160
He said:

129
00:06:43,280 --> 00:06:44,940
Ideals are like stars:

130
00:06:45,300 --> 00:06:47,660
You will not succeed in touching them with your hands,

131
00:06:48,260 --> 00:06:49,760
but, like the seafaring man

132
00:06:49,760 --> 00:06:51,620
on the ocean desert of waters,

133
00:06:52,120 --> 00:06:53,700
You choose them as your guides

134
00:06:54,040 --> 00:06:55,820
and following them you reach your destiny.

135
00:06:56,300 --> 00:06:58,880
This reminds me of a story of

136
00:06:58,880 --> 00:07:00,640
some years ago,

137
00:07:00,640 --> 00:07:03,280
when I was on the Chesapeake Bay

138
00:07:03,280 --> 00:07:05,540
and we were steering a replica

139
00:07:05,540 --> 00:07:07,560
of a 17th century ship,

140
00:07:07,860 --> 00:07:08,560
the Half Moon,

141
00:07:09,580 --> 00:07:11,120
the Henry Hudson ship,

142
00:07:11,120 --> 00:07:14,960
down from Wilmington, Delaware,

143
00:07:15,180 --> 00:07:16,700
down to Washington DC.

144
00:07:17,500 --> 00:07:19,640
Now, this ship didn't have a steering wheel,

145
00:07:19,640 --> 00:07:21,860
like most ships.

146
00:07:22,100 --> 00:07:23,160
It didn't have a helm,

147
00:07:23,160 --> 00:07:25,420
like you're familiar with seeing.

148
00:07:25,420 --> 00:07:28,620
It had this kind of devilish

149
00:07:28,700 --> 00:07:30,800
old, primitive device

150
00:07:30,800 --> 00:07:32,360
attached to the rudder

151
00:07:32,360 --> 00:07:33,640
called a whip stave,

152
00:07:34,840 --> 00:07:35,900
And the steersman

153
00:07:35,900 --> 00:07:38,360
stands in this little doghouse

154
00:07:38,360 --> 00:07:39,640
on the after deck

155
00:07:39,640 --> 00:07:41,240
with no view of the water at all.

156
00:07:41,440 --> 00:07:41,680
I mean

157
00:07:41,760 --> 00:07:42,340
you really

158
00:07:42,480 --> 00:07:43,580
you can't see

159
00:07:43,580 --> 00:07:45,180
what's ahead of you,

160
00:07:45,600 --> 00:07:47,780
You can't see what's beside you

161
00:07:48,160 --> 00:07:49,380
And the directions

162
00:07:49,380 --> 00:07:51,160
have to be relayed

163
00:07:51,160 --> 00:07:51,980
by an officer

164
00:07:51,980 --> 00:07:52,880
conning the ship

165
00:07:52,880 --> 00:07:54,000
above the doghouse

166
00:07:54,000 --> 00:07:55,100
to the steersman

167
00:07:55,100 --> 00:07:56,500
who you know

168
00:07:56,760 --> 00:07:58,340
will be watching a compass

169
00:07:58,340 --> 00:08:00,860
and swings the whip stave around

170
00:08:00,860 --> 00:08:01,960
to adjust the course.

171
00:08:02,660 --> 00:08:03,920
It's not an easy system-

172
00:08:04,360 --> 00:08:05,280
You can tell

173
00:08:05,280 --> 00:08:07,020
why ships are not built today

174
00:08:07,020 --> 00:08:07,820
with whip staves-

175
00:08:08,280 --> 00:08:09,520
And it's not

176
00:08:09,520 --> 00:08:11,480
a system that lends itself

177
00:08:11,480 --> 00:08:12,860
to pinpoint accuracy.

178
00:08:13,860 --> 00:08:14,740
Staying on course

179
00:08:14,740 --> 00:08:15,880
in that ship

180
00:08:15,880 --> 00:08:17,120
was not really about

181
00:08:17,120 --> 00:08:18,060
following a line,

182
00:08:18,060 --> 00:08:20,500
It was occupying a position

183
00:08:20,500 --> 00:08:21,780
in a wide path.

184
00:08:23,520 --> 00:08:23,860
I mean

185
00:08:24,440 --> 00:08:25,940
ships don't respond quickly.

186
00:08:26,720 --> 00:08:28,420
The con has to anticipate

187
00:08:28,420 --> 00:08:29,440
adjustments to course

188
00:08:29,440 --> 00:08:30,120
far ahead,

189
00:08:30,120 --> 00:08:31,520
accounting for currents

190
00:08:31,520 --> 00:08:32,140
and winds,

191
00:08:32,140 --> 00:08:33,140
and you know

192
00:08:33,220 --> 00:08:34,780
whatever is happening out there.

193
00:08:35,299 --> 00:08:36,280
A skilled mariner

194
00:08:36,280 --> 00:08:37,020
doesn't fight

195
00:08:37,020 --> 00:08:38,440
with the conditions

196
00:08:38,440 --> 00:08:39,140
that he finds.

197
00:08:39,440 --> 00:08:40,740
He learns to integrate them

198
00:08:40,740 --> 00:08:41,659
into the art of steering

199
00:08:41,659 --> 00:08:42,240
his ship.

200
00:08:43,400 --> 00:08:44,120
And scouting is

201
00:08:44,120 --> 00:08:45,280
a lot like that.

202
00:08:45,360 --> 00:08:46,540
It's a wide path

203
00:08:46,540 --> 00:08:47,500
with plenty of room

204
00:08:47,500 --> 00:08:48,380
for course correction

205
00:08:48,380 --> 00:08:50,060
and plenty of allowance

206
00:08:50,060 --> 00:08:50,700
for leeway.

207
00:08:51,740 --> 00:08:52,460
Scout Mastership

208
00:08:52,460 --> 00:08:54,140
isn't the job

209
00:08:54,140 --> 00:08:55,580
so much as directing,

210
00:08:55,580 --> 00:08:57,560
as kind of coaxing

211
00:08:57,560 --> 00:08:58,260
things along,

212
00:08:58,700 --> 00:08:59,620
Not so much

213
00:08:59,620 --> 00:09:00,860
as arriving

214
00:09:00,860 --> 00:09:01,800
at a point

215
00:09:01,800 --> 00:09:03,720
but as traveling,

216
00:09:04,320 --> 00:09:04,720
achieving

217
00:09:05,460 --> 00:09:06,340
and getting there.

218
00:09:07,320 --> 00:09:08,640
It's not so much

219
00:09:08,640 --> 00:09:11,040
what we end up with

220
00:09:11,040 --> 00:09:12,360
as what we do.

221
00:09:13,320 --> 00:09:14,180
Scout Mastership

222
00:09:14,180 --> 00:09:15,740
integrates the influences

223
00:09:15,740 --> 00:09:16,560
of society

224
00:09:16,560 --> 00:09:17,180
and family

225
00:09:17,180 --> 00:09:17,760
and school

226
00:09:17,760 --> 00:09:18,360
and church

227
00:09:18,360 --> 00:09:19,960
to make decent

228
00:09:19,960 --> 00:09:20,700
human beings

229
00:09:20,700 --> 00:09:21,880
while they're in

230
00:09:21,880 --> 00:09:22,480
one of the most

231
00:09:22,480 --> 00:09:23,500
chaotic periods

232
00:09:23,500 --> 00:09:24,640
of their lives. potentially

233
00:09:25,280 --> 00:09:25,760
We're not

234
00:09:25,760 --> 00:09:27,920
working towards goals,

235
00:09:28,300 --> 00:09:29,860
We're shaping destinies.

236
00:09:29,860 --> 00:09:31,200
Scout music,

237
00:09:31,200 --> 00:09:31,300
Scout music,

238
00:09:31,300 --> 00:09:31,320
Scout music,

239
00:09:31,320 --> 00:09:33,680
Scout music.

240
00:09:33,680 --> 00:09:34,240
Help me,

241
00:09:34,240 --> 00:09:35,260
Help me,

242
00:09:35,260 --> 00:09:35,280
Help me.

243
